# Pre-commit hook.
#
# Op-debt fix (Wave 11 batch — multi-agent worktree): when multiple
# agents work in linked worktrees that share the same `.git/`,
# `lint-staged`'s default `git stash --include-untracked --keep-index`
# sweeps in OTHER worktrees' untracked files. Popping the stash then
# lands those files in the wrong tree (or loses them).
#
# Mitigation: run lint-staged with `--no-stash` (lint-staged v15+).
# Trade-off: lint-staged operates on the working-tree copy of each
# staged file, so any unstaged edits to a staged file get linted
# alongside the staged hunks. For `prettier --write` and `eslint --fix`
# this is benign — both are idempotent and the agent re-stages the
# touched files. The win is that NO global stash is taken, so sibling
# worktrees stay untouched.
pnpm exec lint-staged --no-stash
